{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement the Gemfire message-channel binder (U1) against the existing Spring Cloud Stream Binder SPI, using Gemfire regions as the backing message channels: producers write messages via region/function entry operations and consumers receive messages via continuous queries (CQ) and region listeners to achieve low latency.",
    "Support partitioning in the binder using Gemfire partitioned regions with the message partition key as the region key, and support consumer groups via durable subscription/queue semantics so competing consumers share load.",
    "Implement the s-c-d Gemfire SPI (U2) as a Spring Cloud Deployer SPI implementation that orchestrates data microservice modules onto the Gemfire infrastructure using Gemfire function execution to launch and manage module launcher instances across Gemfire servers.",
    "Implement the stream repository (U3) as a StreamDefinitionRepository backed by a replicated Gemfire region so stream definitions are stored and shared within the Gemfire cluster.",
    "Implement the module registry (U4) as a ModuleRegistry backed by a Gemfire replicated region for registering and resolving module coordinates (Maven-style group:artifact:version).",
    "Implement tap support (U7) in the stream deployment runtime using the tap naming convention (tap:stream:<stream-name>.<label>): when a tapped stream is deployed, the binder wires an additional tap output channel on the producing module of the primary pipeline, forking the data without impacting the original stream.",
    "Extend the s-c-dataflow DSL parser and Shell (U8) to accept tap stream definitions of the form ':<stream>.<label> > <modules...>', including validation, stream definition creation, shell commands and completion support.",
    "Write all documentation (U5, U6 and new Gemfire feature docs) in Asciidoc following the existing reference documentation structure, including the direct-binding module-launcher example from U6 and the deployment manifest partition properties for U5.",
    "Use an embedded/locally running Gemfire cluster for integration tests, with test configuration isolated from production configuration."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The Spring Cloud Stream binder SPI, Spring Cloud Data Flow server, deployer SPI, stream DSL and shell already exist; this increment adds Gemfire support on top of these extension points rather than building the frameworks from scratch.",
    "The target stack follows the specification preamble (Spring Framework 6.x, Java 17+) and a Gemfire/Geode version compatible with that stack is used.",
    "A single developer (the author) performs all work; all figures are effort (work-hours), not elapsed calendar time, and exclude waiting for external parties.",
    "Each implementation activity includes coding, self-review and debugging; testing activities include writing and running unit and integration tests.",
    "Gemfire is available for development and testing (embedded in tests); no hardware procurement, production cluster provisioning or operations work is included.",
    "User story U5 is truncated in the specification; it is interpreted as a request to document the deployment manifest with emphasis on partition-related properties and how partitioned streams are deployed.",
    "No web UI changes are required; tap support is limited to the DSL and shell.",
    "Low-latency verification is limited to basic functional and smoke performance tests; full performance benchmarking and tuning are out of scope.",
    "The developer is experienced with Spring and messaging but requires some ramp-up on Gemfire APIs; this learning effort is included in the estimates.",
    "Rework caused by external code review feedback is covered by the code review/refactoring activity; no third-party security audit or formal QA cycle is included."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and technical design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze all eight user stories, design the Gemfire binder architecture (regions, CQ listeners, partitioning, consumer groups), the Gemfire deployer SPI, Gemfire-backed stream repository and module registry, and the tap mechanism (naming conventions, DSL syntax, deployment wiring). Produce design notes and interface sketches.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Development environment and test infrastructure setup",
      "activity_description": "Set up Gemfire dependencies in the build, create embedded Gemfire test configuration and utilities, and adjust the CI build to run the new modules and Gemfire-based tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Gemfire binder core implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Spring Cloud Stream binder backed by Gemfire: provisioning of regions, message producer (region/function writes), message consumer (continuous query / region listener subscriptions), binder configuration properties and auto-configuration, partition support, consumer groups and basic error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 96
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Gemfire binder unit and integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests and integration tests (against embedded Gemfire) covering send/receive, partitioning, consumer groups, error paths and configuration binding.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Gemfire deployer SPI implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Spring Cloud Deployer SPI for Gemfire: deploy/undeploy/status of module launcher instances onto the Gemfire infrastructure via function execution, including deployment manifest handling and passing module arguments/properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 72
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Gemfire deployer SPI tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests for the Gemfire deployer SPI covering deploy, undeploy, status reporting, argument passing and failure scenarios against an embedded Gemfire cluster.",
      "most_likely_effort": 36
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Gemfire stream repository implementation and tests",
      "activity_description": "Implement a StreamDefinitionRepository backed by a replicated Gemfire region (serialization of stream definitions, CRUD operations, duplicate handling) plus unit and integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Gemfire module registry implementation and tests",
      "activity_description": "Implement a ModuleRegistry backed by a Gemfire replicated region for registering, unregistering and resolving module coordinates, plus unit and integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Tap runtime support implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement tap support in the stream deployment runtime: recognize tap stream definitions, create tap output channels on the producing module of the primary pipeline using the tap naming convention, and wire them through the binder so tapped data is forked without affecting the primary stream.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Tap runtime tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests verifying that deploying a tap forks the primary pipeline data to the tap stream and that undeploying or failing taps do not impact the original stream.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U8 - DSL and Shell tap support implementation",
      "activity_description": "Extend the s-c-dataflow DSL grammar and parser to accept tap stream definitions (':<stream>.<label> > modules'), create corresponding stream definitions, and add shell command support, validation and tab-completion for taps.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U8 - DSL and Shell tap support tests",
      "activity_description": "Write parser tests for valid and invalid tap syntax and shell integration tests covering creation, listing and destruction of tap streams.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Deployment manifest documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write reference documentation for the deployment manifest with a dedicated section on partition-related properties and examples of deploying partitioned streams.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Direct binding documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write reference documentation on direct binding of modules, including the module-launcher command-line example from the story, argument passing (--args.N) and aggregate/binding properties, verified by executing the example.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Gemfire feature reference documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the new Gemfire capabilities: binder configuration properties, deployer SPI usage, Gemfire-backed stream repository and module registry, and tap usage with Gemfire, integrated into the existing Asciidoc reference docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end integration testing and defect resolution",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end scenarios combining the new features (Gemfire binder with data flow orchestration, taps over a Gemfire-backed pipeline, direct binding examples), perform smoke performance checks for the low-latency path, and fix defects found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "Code review, refactoring and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Perform final code review and refactoring, clean up configuration and dependencies, update changelog/release notes and prepare the increment for release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 628
  }
}

